      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T06:57:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s weird that this is unused; its usage is also inconsistent, because this is called for every new listener for MdnsSocketManager, but it\u0027s called only the first time for MdnsSocketClient.\n\nI think this indicates that it should actually be different methods: startDiscovery()/stopDiscovery(), and separate ones for notifyNetworkRequested(listener, network) / notifyNetworkUnrequested.\n\nThe current usage is also confusing because the \"listener\" is not actually used as a callback for discovery in startDiscovery, it\u0027s just a token to register/unregister the socket request on the network (so I think \"notifyNetworkRequested\" would be a more appropriate name).\n\nYou could provide a default implementation for notifyNetworkRequested in the interface so you don\u0027t have to add an empty one here",
